# Copy to .env and fill in ONE of the two below (never both) at https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
# TMDB issues two different credential types on that page; they are not interchangeable, and pasting one
# into the other's variable sends the wrong auth method and TMDB rejects it (401).
#
#   TMDB_TOKEN    the long "API Read Access Token" under "API Read Access Token (v4 auth)" — a JWT, ~200+
#                 chars, three dot-separated segments (header.payload.signature). Sent as
#                 `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Preferred: this is what TMDB's own docs recommend now.
#   TMDB_API_KEY  the short "API Key" under "API Key (v3 auth)" — exactly 32 hex characters. Sent as the
#                 `?api_key=` query parameter (only used when TMDB_TOKEN is unset — see tmdb/client.ts).
#
# If TMDB_TOKEN is set, it always wins, regardless of TMDB_API_KEY. If both fields on the settings page look
# confusing: the v4 token is long and has two dots in it; the v3 key is short with no dots.
TMDB_TOKEN=
TMDB_API_KEY=

PORT=4000
# Irrelevant to the mobile app (CORS is a browser mechanism); only matters if a web client is ever added.
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Wishlist storage (libSQL, SQLite-compatible). Local dev/tests need nothing here — the default below is
# a local file, no account. For a deployment whose own disk is wiped on redeploy/restart (e.g. Render's
# free tier), point these at a Turso database instead so the wishlist survives: create one free at
# https://turso.tech, then `turso db show <name> --url` and `turso db tokens create <name>`.
# DATABASE_URL=libsql://<your-db>.turso.io
# DATABASE_AUTH_TOKEN=
DATABASE_URL=file:./data/trackzio.db

# Tuning (defaults shown)
# TMDB_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
# TMDB_RATE_PER_SEC=40
